 126:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/common.h ****  * function also accepts an offset of 0 into a buffer whose pointer is null.
 127:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/common.h ****  * (`p + n` has undefined behavior when `p` is null, even when `n == 0`.
 128:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/common.h ****  * A null pointer is a valid buffer pointer when the size is 0, for example
 129:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/common.h ****  * as the result of `malloc(0)` on some platforms.)
 130:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/common.h ****  *
 131:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/common.h ****  * \param p     Pointer to a buffer of at least n bytes.
 132:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/common.h ****  *              This may be \p NULL if \p n is zero.
 133:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/common.h ****  * \param n     An offset in bytes.
 134:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/common.h ****  * \return      Pointer to offset \p n in the buffer \p p.
